{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1176960-mage-the-ascension-tarot-who-is-the-page-of-cups","id":1176960,"title":"Mage the Ascension Tarot Who Is the Page of Cups?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-18T08:43:20-08:00","id":1176960,"title":"Mage the Ascension Tarot Who Is the Page of Cups?","content":"I have the M20 Art of Mage the Ascension and the Mage the Awakening Tarot PDF. I was wondering what the Page of Cups was in the Mage: the Ascension tarot.<br /> <br /> Cups seem to be tied to the Nephandi and the Primordial Essence per M20 Art of Mage the Ascension and I was wondering if the Page of Cups was a widderslainte. If anyone has a picture of the Mage tarot Page of Cups, that would also be great!<br /> <br /> Thanks for the information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T11:40:15-08:00","id":1177370,"title":"","content":"The page of cups is meant to represent the cauls. The threshold a would be nephandi must cross to invert their avatar and lock them down the path of descent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T17:03:53-08:00","id":1177455,"title":"","content":"Ouch. That is a bad card to draw in Mage then, unless it would be drawn in a way (perhaps reversed since I am not versed in tarot) to say that someone is saved from the cauls.<br /> <br /> Thank you Saikou, you've helped me figure out a plot point in my campaign!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T18:53:37-08:00","id":1177488,"title":"","content":"No problem, I used the cards in my games quite frequently. Bare in mind there are no hard and fast rules for how to interpret them. You can use their tarot meaning divorced from all mageness.<br /> <br /> For example, the page of cups can depict a young person who is intuitive, and emotionally charged. They could be a child, or simply young at heart. It can depict someone at the start of an emotional journey, perhaps a relationship, a creative project, or maybe just a realisation from the heart. The card can also represent joyous surprise, unexpected occurrences which may lead to meaningful encounters.<br /> <br /> Reversed it could speak of sorrow, of the beginning of a painful chapter in one's life. It could be a person who is prone to tantrum and anger, childish or simply sorrowful. Indulgence is a strong theme, especially if it's the starting point for worse behaviour.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you could take it to literally mean what the picture shows, someone in a dream having drunk from a golden chalice. A tree spirit nested deep in the heart of the forest, a being trapped within a nightmare.<br /> <br /> Just have fun with it and don't worry about it being &quot;right&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 01-20-2018, 07:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T17:01:24-08:00","id":1177719,"title":"","content":"I was more thinking of how the various factions fit and the picture. I have another tarot deck I just picked up and the Mage: the Awakening Tarot PDF--the Mage the Ascension deck is available at only collector's prices. In this case, the NPC is a Hermetic trying to build a new City of Pymander and needed to find the Eve to his Adam. . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T05:56:52-08:00","id":1177825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1176960-mage-the-ascension-tarot-who-is-the-page-of-cups?p=1177719#post1177719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was more thinking of how the various factions fit and the picture. I have another tarot deck I just picked up and the Mage: the Awakening Tarot PDF--the Mage the Ascension deck is available at only collector's prices. In this case, the NPC is a Hermetic trying to build a new City of Pymander and needed to find the Eve to his Adam. . .</div> </div> </div> </div>The Awakening deck isn't going to tie in to the Ascension factions at all. I'm not entirely sure what you want to do with these cards, but like I said there are no hard and fast rules so if something fits, then use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T10:11:17-08:00","id":1177876,"title":"","content":"Awakening is indeed not Ascension, but it works with enough themes to provide some ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T00:23:07-08:00","id":1178009,"title":"","content":"It looks a lot like an enfant wraith as well. Newly dead wraiths reside in cocoons, which are also called cauls, where they stay until another wraith (called a reaper) breaks them out. <br /> <br /> The booklet that comes with the cards confirms what Saikou said, though. It does make me think that the cauls of the nephandi and the cauls worn by newly dead wraiths may even be one in the same... food for thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}